---
import LexJoltLayout from '../layouts/LexJoltLayout.astro';
import { brand } from '../config/brand';
---
<LexJoltLayout title="Privacy" description="Privacy policy for LexJolt.">
  <article class="lexjolt-shell lexjolt-section">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="lexjolt-eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="lexjolt-h1 mt-2">Privacy policy</h1>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 leading-7 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
        <p>LexJolt is free and does not require accounts, passwords, payment information, or a premium tier.</p>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50">Browser storage</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">LexJolt stores preferences and local play state in your browser, including recent letters, theme preference, local game scores, streaks, and Daily Jolt status.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50">Analytics</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">LexJolt may use privacy-conscious Plausible analytics when configured for the production domain. Analytics events must not send the raw letters or words you enter.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50">Dictionary information</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">Word solving and most word details use files served directly with LexJolt. If a local detail is not included, LexJolt may request it from an external dictionary service. External availability never controls whether the local solver works.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50">Contact</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">Questions can be sent to <a class="font-semibold text-primary-700 dark:text-primary-200" href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}>{brand.email}</a>.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</LexJoltLayout>
